  <h2>Operator Precedence</h2>

  <p>From highest to lowest precedence:</p>

  <ol>
    <li>Parentheses <code>()</code></li>
    <li>Unary operators <code>not</code>, <code>-</code></li>
    <li>Multiplication, division <code>*</code>, <code>/</code>, <code>%</code></li>
    <li>Addition, subtraction <code>+</code>, <code>-</code></li>
    <li>Comparison <code>=</code>, <code>!=</code>, <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;=</code></li>
    <li>Boolean AND <code>and</code></li>
    <li>Boolean OR <code>or</code></li>
  </ol>

  <p>Use parentheses when precedence is unclear:</p>

  <pre><code>// Clear
(a + b) * c
a and (b or c)

// Ambiguous - use parentheses
a + b * c   // Is this (a + b) * c or a + (b * c)?</code></pre>

